Description: test-service: use a per-process daemon control directory
 test_service_setup() launches gnome-keyring-daemon with a FIXED
 control directory, /tmp/keyring-test.  The setup is shared by all the
 test-dbus-* binaries, which run concurrently under a parallel
 `make check` (TESTSUITEFLAGS=-j48 on the 48-core Athena builder), so
 two daemons collide on the directory, one never appears on the bus,
 and the g_bus_watch_name wait times out:
 .
   ERROR:daemon/dbus/test-service.c:100:test_service_setup:
   assertion failed: (egg_test_wait_until (20000) != FALSE)
   ERROR: test-dbus-portal process failed: -6
 .
 Every other daemon test (test-startup, test-shutdown) already uses a
 unique scratch directory as the control directory; give this shared
 setup a per-pid one too.  Passed on the old low-core builder whose
 narrower test parallelism rarely overlapped the binaries.
Origin: vendor, Athena-Build
Forwarded: no
Author: Athena-Build
Last-Update: 2026-11-08
---
--- a/daemon/dbus/test-service.c
+++ b/daemon/dbus/test-service.c
@@ -67,16 +67,25 @@
 	GVariant *output;
 	gchar **env;
 
+	/* The control directory must be unique per test process: the
+	 * test-dbus-* binaries share this setup and run concurrently under
+	 * a parallel make check, and daemons colliding on a fixed
+	 * /tmp/keyring-test leave one of them unable to come up, timing
+	 * out the service watch below. */
+	static gchar control_directory[64];
 	const gchar *args[] = {
 		BUILDDIR "/gnome-keyring-daemon",
 		"--foreground",
 		"--control-directory",
-		"/tmp/keyring-test",
+		control_directory,
 		"--components",
 		"secrets",
 		NULL,
 	};
 
+	g_snprintf (control_directory, sizeof (control_directory),
+	            "/tmp/keyring-test-%d", (int) getpid ());
+
 	test->bus_name = g_strdup_printf ("org.gnome.keyring.Test.t%d", getpid ());
 
 	test->watch_id = g_bus_watch_name (G_BUS_TYPE_SESSION, test->bus_name,
